  "issue_title": "Audit consumers of reconstructed label fields",
  "issue_body": "**Context**\nThis PR makes issue/PR labels conditional historical data: `labels` is only meaningful when `labels_as_of_t` is true. Any benchmark, prompt construction, or analysis code that treats an empty `labels` list as historical truth can now silently misread unavailable timeline data as \"no labels at T\".\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n- [ ] Search all consumers of frozen GitHub context for direct reads of issue/PR `labels`.\n- [ ] Update consumers to check `labels_as_of_t` before treating labels as historically exact.\n- [ ] Add a regression test covering `labels: []` with `labels_as_of_t: false`.\n- [ ] Document the consumer contract near the frozen context schema or architecture notes.\n\n**Pointers**: `benchmark/github_context.py::_collect_open_at`, `benchmark/github_context.py::_labels_at`, `tests/test_github_context.py`, `docs/architecture.md`",
